WEBVTT

00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:14.627
Where does the left crease come from? The B-spline was drawn through traced points, and at its end it turns a corner into the vertical line—the outline is only G0, so the extruded surface kinks too

00:00:15.627 --> 00:00:22.877
Double-click the side outline sketch and make both ends of the B-spline tangent to their neighbouring lines

00:00:22.877 --> 00:00:34.627
First delete the coincident constraint at the end (select it in the list, press Delete)—an endpoint tangency already includes coincidence, so keeping it would be redundant

00:00:34.627 --> 00:00:46.627
Then select the B-spline's endpoint, Ctrl-select the line's endpoint and click Tangent—once at each end

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:54.632
Both ends are tangent: the outline is now G1—continuous direction, no corners

00:00:54.632 --> 00:01:06.632
Back on the solid, the left crease is gone and the curve blends into the side. G0 is position, G1 adds direction, G2 adds curvature—the smoothest reflections
